---
import { Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro'
---

<LegalPage
  description="How the Lumen website, playground apps, packages, and public MCP server handle information."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  title="Privacy policy"
  updatedAt="November 6, 2026"
>
  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers the Lumen UI documentation website, native Lumen Playground applications,
    the Lumen for Figma plugin, published packages, and the public Lumen MCP server published by Santiago Molina. Lumen is an
    open-source design system and does not require a user account.
  </p>

  <h2>Playground applications</h2>
  <p>
    The Lumen Playground applications are offline component catalogs. They do not require an
    account, display advertising, include analytics or tracking SDKs, request sensitive device
    permissions, or collect, retain, or share personal data. Interactive form values, appearance
    choices, and demonstration settings remain on the device only for the current app session.
    Opening documentation, support, or privacy links leaves the app and uses the selected browser,
    whose provider may process requests under its own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="figma-plugin">Lumen for Figma</h2>
  <p>
    The plugin reads the selected design’s visible text, layer structure, component properties,
    layout, and color variable names inside Figma to generate code and a handoff. It has no network
    access, calls no AI model, and sends no design data or usage analytics to Lumen. A registered
    build can add a relaunch shortcut to the document.
  </p>
  <p>
    Copying code or saving a file places the export on your device. Only share an export with
    a coding agent or another recipient after reviewing it for private design text. The plugin
    does not share the export for you. Figma and any service you choose to use have their own
    privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Information processed by the MCP server</h2>
  <p>
    MCP requests can include a component name, framework or platform selection, catalog manifest,
    and natural-language search query. The server uses that input only to return public Lumen
    documentation, source contracts, recipes, tokens, and rules. The application does not use MCP
    requests for advertising, profiling, or model training.
  </p>

  <h2>Operational data</h2>
  <p>
    Hosting and security infrastructure may process limited technical data such as an IP address,
    timestamp, requested path, response status, and user agent to deliver the service, enforce rate
    limits, investigate abuse, and maintain reliability. Lumen does not intentionally request or
    store account credentials, repository contents, authorization tokens, or personal profile data.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage and sharing</h2>
  <p>
    The MCP application does not persist tool arguments or responses. Operational logs, if produced
    by the hosting infrastructure, are retained only as long as needed for security and reliability.
    Lumen does not sell personal information. Technical data may be processed by infrastructure
    providers only to host, secure, and operate the service or when required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can use the published npm package over stdio instead of the hosted MCP endpoint. You may
    also stop using or disable the plugin at any time. For a privacy question, open a
    <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/lumen/issues/new/choose" newTab>
      Lumen support request
    </Link>
    without including sensitive information; a maintainer can arrange a private follow-up when
    necessary.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Material changes will be published on this page with a new update date. The current policy is
    available at this URL for app-store, plugin-review, and user reference.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
